Before a private-server installation has a verified Pully connection, the shared
connection screen MUST explain its next step and offer working Retry and Server
settings actions. It MUST distinguish a failed response from an empty connected
Inbox and MUST NOT show raw responses, parser/native exception details or imply
GitHub/account authorization from HTML alone. A returning verified account MUST
retain offline access. Public-capable hosts MUST offer public browsing as the
ordinary signed-out path rather than requiring operator Access credentials.
Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 reinstall screenshot and follow-up asking for personal
GitHub sign-in plus public-repository browsing without sign-in.
